# Input default (LOCKED)

When creating an input, use the lock in `src/Products/PinoyBusinessPOS/ExItS.PinoyBusinessPOS.React/src/features/ui-standards/input-global-default.ts`.

The locked command is `ext input primary outlined`. Intent is primary (`INPUT_GLOBAL_DEFAULT_INTENT`). Appearance is outlined (`INPUT_GLOBAL_DEFAULT_APPEARANCE`). Shape and density stay Standard unless the user names them.

The Form Components submenu **Input** playground has a lock labeled **default global**. That lock is what a new input is expected to use.

Use the locked ExItS input. Do not pick a different intent or appearance unless the user names one. On `/ui-standards`, the locked input is `PlaygroundTextField`, and the locked search is `PlaygroundSearchField`.

## Type (LOCKED)

The lock in `field-typography-global-default.ts` (same folder) covers every appearance except **Label above**:

- Label: `FIELD_GLOBAL_LABEL_SIZE` = **13px** (`--qinput-label-size`). It is the same size inside the field and when raised. `FIELD_GLOBAL_FLOAT_SCALE` = 1, so the raised label slides up and does not shrink.
- Typed text: `FIELD_GLOBAL_TEXT_SIZE` = **14px**.
- Density changes the typed text only. It does not change the label.
- Label above keeps its own static 14px label (`FIELD_GLOBAL_STACKED_LABEL_SIZE`). Do not touch it unless the user names Label above.

Change these sizes only when the user asks. Update `field-typography-global-default.ts`, the tokens in `globals.css`, and `field-typography-global-default.test.ts` together.
